{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1322916-what-happens-to-a-kindred-embraced-while-on-mood-altering-meds","id":1322916,"title":"What happens to a Kindred embraced while on mood-altering meds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-08T02:58:46-07:00","id":1322916,"title":"What happens to a Kindred embraced while on mood-altering meds?","content":"Doesn\u2019t have to be anything dramatic, maybe they just took an SSRI to function a little better.<br /> <br /> Do they still feel or act different based on the presence/absence of the med? Does it stick around in their system until they burn off the Vitae, or wear off like it would in a mortal, or just fail to affect them at all? When they first wake as Kindred, are they going to feel like their medicated self, or their unmedicated self?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T04:09:48-07:00","id":1322924,"title":"","content":"This gets into a tricky area. Being a vampire usually heals injuries and diseases, but I'm pretty sure we put vampires in the books who carry issues from their normal lives. But are mental illnesses problems in that sense? It gets a lot into player comfort levels.<br /> <br /> That said, in my games I've always allowed vampires to mix a drug with their own blood, then drink or inject it. Which would allow them to medicate.<br /> <br /> (Mind you, many drugs just don't <i>work</i> on Kindred physiology. Like I said, tricky area.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T17:43:59-07:00","id":1323085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1322916-what-happens-to-a-kindred-embraced-while-on-mood-altering-meds?p=1322924#post1322924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gets into a tricky area. Being a vampire usually heals injuries and diseases, but I'm pretty sure we put vampires in the books who carry issues from their normal lives. But are mental illnesses problems in that sense? It gets a lot into player comfort levels.<br /> <br /> That said, in my games I've always allowed vampires to mix a drug with their own blood, then drink or inject it. Which would allow them to medicate.<br /> <br /> (Mind you, many drugs just don't <i>work</i> on Kindred physiology. Like I said, tricky area.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you usually simulate it by roleplay? Since there is no hard and fast rules for drug intoxication in core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T18:40:32-07:00","id":1323096,"title":"","content":"Malkavian bloodline? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}